{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3nf53hTjojCoz1ratyk","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `wholsale` to `wholesale` in the October, November and December files and committed it as one commit, `2fae178`. Reverting that commit undoes the whole fix.\n\n- **What changed:** one row in each of `data/2025-10.csv`, `data/2025-11.csv` and `data/2025-12.csv`. A search for the misspelling found those three rows and nothing else in the tracked files, so no other table or output file needed fixing.\n- **Check:** `scripts/check.sh` printed OK before the commit.\n- **Commit prefix:** `CLAUDE.md` wants the data month first. The commit touches three months, so I used `2025-12`, the latest of them. Say so if you'd rather use a different prefix, since the import log groups by it.\n- **Not touched:** `inbox/2025-12.csv` has the same misspelling, but `.gitignore` excludes `inbox/`, so it isn't part of the repo. If you re-import from it, the typo will come back, so tell me if you want it fixed there too.\n- **Still untracked:** `data/2026-01.csv`, as you asked.","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":364,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":445,"cache_read_input_tokens":20351,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":445,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-42>","timestamp":"2026-11-15T00:44:18.472Z","request_id":"gen-1794703455-5DqjXuwphqAXdYT7V3LJ"}
